# Design system rules

Sources: Figma Design System V2 ↔ `tokens/*.tokens.json` ↔ shadcn ↔ Storybook ↔ prototypes.

## Tokens

- Prefer semantic tokens; never hardcode product colors in components
- Preserve primitive → semantic → component relationships and Figma aliases where possible
- Support Light/Dark when present in Figma
- Generate CSS from token JSON; do not hand-maintain duplicate values
- Never silently change token semantics — log in `docs/decisions.md`
- During migration: inspect Figma first, gap-report before architecture changes, preserve Figma naming unless documented

## Figma MCP

- Inspect file, variables, collections, and component conventions before create/edit
- Reuse existing structures; do not recreate tokens/components that already exist
- When Figma and code disagree, report the discrepancy before choosing a winner

## shadcn/ui

- Foundation for code, not visual source of truth
- Customize via our tokens and APIs
- Do not copy arbitrary shadcn colors, hardcode `bg-blue-500` when a semantic token exists, duplicate components, or change generated APIs without documenting

## Components & Storybook

- Keep Figma concepts and code APIs aligned (variant, size, state, icon, loading, etc.)
- Production components need stories: default, variants, sizes, hover/focus/disabled/loading, error, long content, a11y edges
- Verify in Storybook; screenshots alone are insufficient

## Accessibility

Preserve keyboard nav, visible focus, semantic HTML, accessible names, contrast, disabled semantics, target size, and Radix/shadcn a11y behavior.
